# Local WordPress (Playground)

This repo boots a real WordPress site for Cloud Agents. Use it instead of stand-in HTML pages when verifying front-end, theme, CSS, or PHP changes in `forgedseo-core`.

`wp-now` is deprecated. The environment uses `@wp-playground/cli` (PHP.wasm + SQLite, no Docker, no MariaDB, no apt PHP, no WP-CLI).

## URL and login

- Site: `http://127.0.0.1:8080`
- Admin: `http://127.0.0.1:8080/wp-admin` — `admin` / `admin`
- Port `8080` is exposed from `.cursor/environment.json`.

The Cloud Agent `install` step runs `scripts/cloud-agent-setup.sh`. The `wordpress` terminal runs `scripts/cloud-agent-start.sh` on boot. If the site is not up yet, start it:

```bash
bash scripts/cloud-agent-setup.sh
bash scripts/cloud-agent-start.sh
```

Wait until `curl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' http://127.0.0.1:8080/` returns `200` before screenshotting. The public site starts logged out (visitor view). Log in at `/wp-admin` when you need admin.

## Live plugin mount

`src/wp-content/plugins/forgedseo-core` is mounted into the Playground site. Edits in the repo show up on reload. Do not copy the plugin into `$HOME/forgedseo-wp-dev`. Do not bump the plugin version for environment work.

The Playground-only seed plugin lives under `scripts/playground/forgedseo-dev-seed/` and is mounted at runtime. Never put it inside `src/wp-content/plugins/forgedseo-core`.

## Verify on this site

Screenshot the local site (homepage plus any inner page you changed) at desktop and mobile widths. That is the required proof that forgedseo-core CSS, JS, block markup, and PHP ran without warnings.

Do not build mock HTML pages that only load `forgedseo.css` / `forgedseo.js` as a substitute.

Useful paths: `/`, `/service/`, `/enterprise/`, `/about/`, `/blog/`.

Final layout checks still happen on the real site (`https://forgedseo.com`). Playground uses Twenty Twenty-Five (same as production) but does not include LiteSpeed Cache, Hostinger-bundled plugins, Site Kit, or other services that need API keys. Treat local screenshots as proof of the plugin change; confirm header/footer/pixel match on production when that matters.

## Reseed

Content is seeded once (option `forgedseo_dev_seeded`). To apply seed changes:

- Logged in: visit `http://127.0.0.1:8080/?forgedseo_reseed=1`
- Wipe SQLite + WordPress files and boot clean: `bash scripts/cloud-agent-start.sh --reset`

`bash scripts/cloud-agent-start.sh --warmup` starts the site, waits until `http://localhost:8080` responds, then returns (used by setup).

## What this is not

Production (`https://forgedseo.com`) also runs LiteSpeed Cache, Site Kit by Google, and Hostinger-bundled plugins. Those are omitted here (cache fights live reload; Site Kit needs API keys; Hostinger plugins are not on WordPress.org). All in One SEO is installed because forgedseo-core writes to `aioseo_posts`.

Never write to production from this environment. Never commit Playground state, SQLite files, or credentials.
